title="Johnson He">Johnson He</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><fr:p>"A <fr:em>topos</fr:em> is a category <fr:tex
display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {E}]]></fr:tex> such that
        <fr:ul><fr:li>1. <fr:tex
display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {E}]]></fr:tex> has all finite limits,</fr:li>
            <fr:li>2. <fr:tex
display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {E}]]></fr:tex> has a subobject classifier,</fr:li>
            <fr:li>3. <fr:tex
display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {E}]]></fr:tex> has all exponentials.</fr:li></fr:ul>
        This compact definition proves to be amazingly rich in consequences:
        it can be shown for instance that topoi also have all finite colimits, and that every slice category of a topos is again a topos."</fr:p></fr:mainmatter><fr:backmatter /></fr:tree><fr:tree
